  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/tilapia-buettikoferi-2/",
      "html": "<p>Tilapia buettikoferi originates from western Africa (Guinea, Liberia, Sierra Leone).</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "aquariumSize",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/tilapia-buettikoferi-2/",
      "html": "<p>Tilapia buettikoferi attains a maximum length of 30-40 cm and is one of the largest species of the genus. It needs really large tanks.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/tilapia-buettikoferi-2/",
      "html": "<p>The species is omnivorous and the diet should contain larger amounts of plant material.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/tilapia-buettikoferi-2/",
      "html": "<p>In real (!) large tanks this species is an absolute eyecatcher and reminds one of the Tanganyika humphead (Cyphotilapia frontosa) due to its calm temper.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/tilapia-buettikoferi-2/",
      "html": "<p>T. buettikoferi is an openbrooder with biparental care and very productive.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/tilapia-buettikoferi-2/",
      "html": "<p>There is some chaos with respect to the scientific naming of this species. The specific name is sometimes spelled buttikoferi (in the original description from 1894 it is spelled with Umlaut \"ü\", which is not allowed according to the international rules of nomenclature). Moreover the species is sometimes placed in the genus Heterotilapia (an invalid genus name) or Herotilapia (a generic name used for Central American cichlids). Both are wrong.</p>"
    }
  ],
